      "explanation": "<strong>Correct: A.</strong> FLOP/s helps characterize arithmetic throughput. Given the same 1-billion-FLOP task, completing it in 0.1 seconds implies about 10 GFLOP/s; in 0.2 seconds, about 5 GFLOP/s. Actual latency also depends on memory, software and overhead, so theoretical peak performance is not a guarantee."
