      "tag": "Count vs. rate",
      "stem": "Layer 3: How are floating-point operations counted, and what is the difference between FLOPs, FLOPS, and FLOP/s?",
      "figure": "<div class=\"fl-diagram\"><span class=\"fl-eyebrow\">03 · terminology</span><h3>One calculation, three labels: amount, rate, and unit</h3><div class=\"fl-canvas\">\n<div class=\"fl-triple\">\n<section class=\"fl-term\"><span>FLOPs</span><strong>How much work?</strong><div class=\"fl-term-main\">8 × 8 = 64</div><small>Example: an operation count</small><i class=\"fl-term-sign\">COUNT</i></section>\n<section class=\"fl-term\"><span>FLOPS</span><strong>How fast?</strong><div class=\"fl-term-main\">64 in 2 s</div><small>32 floating-point operations each second</small><i class=\"fl-term-sign\">RATE</i></section>\n<section class=\"fl-term\"><span>FLOP/s</span><strong>Same rate unit</strong><div class=\"fl-term-main\">32 FLOP/s</div><small>Sometimes written as FLOPS</small><i class=\"fl-term-sign\">UNIT</i></section>\n</div>\n<div class=\"fl-mac-lesson\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 660 110\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A fused multiply add calculates two times three plus four; counts two operations by the multiply plus add convention\"><rect width=\"660\" height=\"110\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#f0f8fb\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"37\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#34687d\" font-weight=\"850\">2 × 3 + 4 = 10</text><path d=\"M310 43H383\" stroke=\"#d28a56\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M373 34l10 9-10 9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#d28a56\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"482\" cy=\"52\" r=\"37\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#80bec6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"482\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#1d6e73\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"900\">2</text><text x=\"482\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1d6e73\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FLOPs</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b8592\">1 multiply + 1 add → 2 floating-point operations</text></svg></div>\n</div><p class=\"fl-note\"><strong>Counting conventions matter:</strong> This lesson uses the common convention that a multiply-add contributes 2 FLOPs; other profiling tools (e.g., fvcore) can count one fused multiply-add as one operation.</p></div>",
      "answer": "d",
      "options": [
