      "explanation": "<strong>Correct: D.</strong> FLOPs (plural) usually means a number of floating-point operations; FLOPS and FLOP/s describe operations each second. Under a common compute convention one multiply plus one add counts as 2 FLOPs. Some tools use a different convention for a fused multiply-add (FMA), so compare like with like."
