      "tag": "Measure in Python",
      "stem": "Layer 5: How are FLOPs measured in Python using PyTorch profiling tools, and how is computational performance benchmarked?",
      "figure": "<div class=\"fl-diagram\"><span class=\"fl-eyebrow\">05 · Python profiling</span><h3>Count supported operations, then time a warmed-up matrix multiplication</h3><div class=\"fl-canvas\"><div class=\"fl-profile\">\n<div class=\"fl-code\"><div class=\"fl-code-top\"><i></i><i></i><i></i> pytorch_profile.py</div><pre><code>import time\nimport torch\nfrom torch.profiler import profile, ProfilerActivity\n\ndevice = &quot;cuda&quot; if torch.cuda.is_available() else &quot;cpu&quot;\na = torch.randn(512, 512, device=device)\nb = torch.randn(512, 512, device=device)\n\nactivities = [ProfilerActivity.CPU]\nif device == &quot;cuda&quot;:\n    activities.append(ProfilerActivity.CUDA)\n\nwith profile(activities=activities, with_flops=True) as p:\n    result = a @ b\nestimated_flops = sum(e.flops or 0 for e in p.key_averages())\nprint(&quot;profile-estimated FLOPs:&quot;, estimated_flops)\n\nfor _ in range(5):\n    result = a @ b\nif device == &quot;cuda&quot;: torch.cuda.synchronize()\nstart = time.perf_counter()\nrepeats = 25\nfor _ in range(repeats):\n    result = a @ b\nif device == &quot;cuda&quot;: torch.cuda.synchronize()\nseconds = (time.perf_counter() - start) / repeats\nprint(&quot;average seconds:&quot;, seconds)\nprint(&quot;approx achieved GFLOP/s:&quot;, 2*512**3/seconds/1e9)</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"fl-profile-aside\">\n<div class=\"fl-profile-title\">WHAT THE MEASUREMENTS MEAN</div>\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 310 212\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Profiler arithmetic count and elapsed time combined to estimate achieved floating point operations per second\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"8\" width=\"278\" height=\"190\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d9e6ed\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#52748a\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\">Estimated work</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"65\" fill=\"#256b89\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\">2 × 512³ ≈ 268 M</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#8eabbc\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"34\" y=\"108\" fill=\"#52748a\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\">Measured time</text><rect x=\"36\" y=\"121\" width=\"238\" height=\"14\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e5eef3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"36\" y=\"121\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#6db5be\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"158\" fill=\"#266b7b\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\">FLOP/s = work / seconds</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"181\" fill=\"#ad7150\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\">CUDA timing requires sync</text></svg>\n<div class=\"fl-alert\">Profiler <code>with_flops=True</code> supports a limited set of operators, including matrix multiplication and 2D convolution. It is an estimate, not a full hardware instruction count.</div>\n</div></div></div><p class=\"fl-note\"><strong>Benchmark correctly:</strong> warm up first, synchronize GPU work before and after timing, and run several repeats. PyTorch profiler can add overhead; measure timing separately from profiler instrumentation.</p></div>",
      "answer": "a",
      "options": [
