>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#5d7f90\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"start\">↑</text>\n<text x=\"17\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#5d7f90\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rate</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#678796\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"start\">More compute units won't help</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n<div class=\"fl-precision\"><div class=\"fl-profile-title\">WHAT THE NUMBERS MEASURE</div>\n<div class=\"fl-prec-line\"><strong>FP32</strong><span>32-bit floating point</span><i></i></div>\n<div class=\"fl-prec-line\"><strong>FP16 / BF16</strong><span>16-bit floating point formats</span><i></i></div>\n<div class=\"fl-prec-line\"><strong>INT8</strong><span>8-bit integer operations</span><i class=\"is-int\"></i></div>\n<div class=\"fl-prec-warning\">INT8 performance is normally quoted as <strong>integer OPS/s or TOPS</strong>, not floating-point FLOP/s.</div></div></div><div class=\"fl-chip-row\"><div><span class=\"fl-chip-icon\">C</span><strong>CPU</strong><small>General processing</small></div><div><span class=\"fl-chip-icon\">G</span><strong>GPU</strong><small>Highly parallel arithmetic</small></div><div><span class=\"fl-chip-icon\">T</span><strong>TPU</strong><small>Tensor acceleration</small></div><div><span class=\"fl-chip-icon\">E</span><strong>EDGE</strong><small>Power / thermal limits</small></div></div></div><p class=\"fl-note\"><strong>Never compare unlike specifications blindly:</strong> advertised peak TFLOP/s changes with FP32, FP16, BF16, matrix-engine usage, sparsity assumptions, device utilization, and the real model workload.</p></div>",
