xt-anchor=\"start\">Base model</text><circle cx=\"267\" cy=\"180\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#4c9f9f\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"280\" y=\"172\" fill=\"#45657c\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\">Quantized</text><circle cx=\"390\" cy=\"206\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6f87c3\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"403\" y=\"198\" fill=\"#45657c\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\">Batched</text><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"224\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#69ad80\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"253\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#45657c\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\">Pruned</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"164\" fill=\"#648094\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Latency ↓</text>\n</svg>\n</div><div class=\"fl-deploy-cards\">\n<div class=\"fl-deploy\"><span>01</span><strong>Quantize</strong><small>Smaller precision; benchmark accuracy + real kernels</small></div><div class=\"fl-deploy\"><span>02</span><strong>Prune</strong><small>Fewer useful operations only if hardware can exploit sparsity</small></div><div class=\"fl-deploy\"><span>03</span><strong>Batch</strong><small>Better throughput may raise per-request wait time</small></div><div class=\"fl-deploy\"><span>04</span><strong>Energy</strong><small>Track joules per request as well as speed</small></div>\n</div></div><div class=\"fl-decision\"><div>MODEL QUALITY <b>✓</b></div><span>+</span><div>LATENCY <b>ms</b></div><span>+</span><div>THROUGHPUT <b>req/s</b></div><span>+</span><div>ENERGY <b>J/req</b></div></div></div><p class=\"fl-note\"><strong>Measure on the target device with representative inputs.</strong> Lower estimated FLOPs may not mean lower latency if memory, kernels, device utilization, or batching dominate; energy and accuracy matter too.</p></div>",
